IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- INSTRUMENT: Telecommunications (Cable Detection Workers) Regulations (Cap. 323, Rg 4), 2002 Revised Edition, with its two amending
-- instruments S 477/2005 (21 July 2005) and S 220/2007 (1 June 2007).  Made under section 74 of the Act (section 97 in the 2020 Revised
-- Edition); the licensing of cable detection workers is Part 5 of the Act (s 35).  It concerns people who dig, not people who receive broadcasts.
-- Texts: TA1999-RG4, TA1999-RG4-S477-2005, TA1999-RG4-S220-2007 under
-- subjects/sg/telecommunications-cable-detection-workers-regulations/registers/source-bundle/.
-- A date before 1 January 2003 answers NOTHING for the 2002 Revised Edition form (its start date is not printed), as in the other instruments.

§ `Rg 4 regulations 2 to 5: definitions, application, qualifications, licence`

-- src:TA1999-RG4:61 | 2. In these Regulations, unless the context otherwise requires —
-- src:TA1999-RG4:62 | "licence" means a licence granted by the Authority permitting a person to perform
-- src:TA1999-RG4:63 | such telecommunication cable detection work as is specified in the
-- src:TA1999-RG4:64 | licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:65 | "licensee" means the holder of a valid licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:66 | "register" means the register of licensees maintained under regulation 6.
@ref Rg 4 reg 2 (src:TA1999-RG4:61-66)
GIVEN `the holder holds a valid licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 2: the person is a "licensee"` MEANS
    `the holder holds a valid licence`

GIVEN `it is a licence granted by the Authority permitting a person to perform the telecommunication cable detection work specified in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 2: this is a "licence"` MEANS
    `it is a licence granted by the Authority permitting a person to perform the telecommunication cable detection work specified in it`

-- src:TA1999-RG4:72 | 3. —(1) An application for a licence and an application to renew a licence shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG4:73 | (a) be made to the Authority in such form as the Authority may determine; and
-- src:TA1999-RG4:74 | (b) be accompanied by the appropriate fee specified in the Schedule.
-- src:TA1999-RG4:75 | (2) An application to renew a licence shall be made not later than one month before the
-- src:TA1999-RG4:76 | date of expiry of the licence.
@ref Rg 4 reg 3 (src:TA1999-RG4:72-76)
GIVEN `the application is made to the Authority in the form it determined` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is accompanied by the appropriate fee specified in the Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months before the expiry of the licence that an application to renew is made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 3: the application for a licence, or its renewal, is as the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the application is made to the Authority in the form it determined` AND `it is accompanied by the appropriate fee specified in the Schedule` AND (`months before the expiry of the licence that an application to renew is made` AT LEAST 1)

-- src:TA1999-RG4:79 | 4. —(1) No licence shall be granted to any person unless the Authority is satisfied that —
-- src:TA1999-RG4:80 | (a) he holds an Industrial Technician Certificate, or a National Technical
-- src:TA1999-RG4:81 | Certificate Grade 2, issued by the Institute of Technical Education, Singapore, has
-- src:TA1999-RG4:82 | not less than 3 GCE ‘O’ level passes or holds such other educational
-- src:TA1999-RG4:83 | qualifications as may be acceptable to the Authority;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:84 | (b) he has not less than one year’s relevant practical experience in building
-- src:TA1999-RG4:85 | construction, building services, civil engineering or structural engineering
-- src:TA1999-RG4:86 | construction or such other relevant experience for such duration as may be
-- src:TA1999-RG4:87 | acceptable to the Authority; and
-- src:TA1999-RG4:88 | (c) he has successfully completed a course in telecommunication cable detection
-- src:TA1999-RG4:89 | work approved by the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG4:90 | (2) The Authority may refuse to grant a licence to any person whose licence has
-- src:TA1999-RG4:91 | previously been cancelled.
@ref Rg 4 reg 4 (src:TA1999-RG4:79-91)
GIVEN `the person holds an Industrial Technician Certificate or a National Technical Certificate Grade 2, has not less than 3 GCE 'O' level passes, or holds other educational qualifications acceptable to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has not less than one year's relevant practical experience in building construction, building services, civil engineering or structural engineering construction, or other relevant experience acceptable to the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has successfully completed a course in telecommunication cable detection work approved by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 4(1): the Authority may grant the licence` MEANS
        `the person holds an Industrial Technician Certificate or a National Technical Certificate Grade 2, has not less than 3 GCE 'O' level passes, or holds other educational qualifications acceptable to the Authority`
    AND `the person has not less than one year's relevant practical experience in building construction, building services, civil engineering or structural engineering construction, or other relevant experience acceptable to the Authority`
    AND `the person has successfully completed a course in telecommunication cable detection work approved by the Authority`

GIVEN `the person's licence has previously been cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 4(2): the Authority may refuse to grant a licence to the person` MEANS
    `the person's licence has previously been cancelled`

-- src:TA1999-RG4:94 | 5. A licence shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG4:95 | (a) be signed by an officer authorised by the Authority;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:96 | (b) be valid for such period as the Authority may determine unless cancelled or
-- src:TA1999-RG4:97 | suspended in accordance with these Regulations; and
-- src:TA1999-RG4:98 | (c) be subject to such terms and conditions as the Authority may, from time to
-- src:TA1999-RG4:99 | time, determine.
@ref Rg 4 reg 5 (src:TA1999-RG4:94-99)
GIVEN `the licence is signed by an officer authorised by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licence has not been cancelled or suspended in accordance with these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 5: the licence is validly issued and is valid` MEANS
    `the licence is signed by an officer authorised by the Authority` AND `the licence has not been cancelled or suspended in accordance with these Regulations`

§ `Rg 4 regulations 6 to 14: the register, duties, cancellation, penalties; the Schedule`

-- src:TA1999-RG4:105 | 6. The Authority shall maintain a register of licensed telecommunication cable detection
-- src:TA1999-RG4:106 | workers which shall, in respect of each licensee, contain the following particulars:
-- src:TA1999-RG4:107 | (a) the full name and address of the licensee as provided by the licensee;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:108 | (b) the date on which the licence was granted and the date of expiry;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:109 | (c) the registration number of the licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:110 | (d) whether the licensee has been convicted of any offence under the Act;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:111 | (e) whether the licence has been suspended or cancelled or whether an application
-- src:TA1999-RG4:112 | to renew the licence has been refused; and
-- src:TA1999-RG4:113 | (f) such other particulars as the Authority thinks fit.
-- src:TA1999-RG4:115 | Inspection of register
-- src:TA1999-RG4:116 | 7. —(1) Any person may, upon payment of the appropriate fee specified in the Schedule,
-- src:TA1999-RG4:117 | inspect the register during the office hours of the Authority.
-- src:TA1999-RG4:118 | (2) The Authority may provide a certified true copy of an entry in the register to any
-- src:TA1999-RG4:119 | person on payment of the appropriate fee specified in the Schedule.
@ref Rg 4 reg 6 and reg 7 (src:TA1999-RG4:105-119)
GIVEN `the register records the licensee's full name and address, the date the licence was granted and its date of expiry, its registration number, whether the licensee has been convicted of any offence under the Act, whether the licence has been suspended or cancelled or an application to renew refused, and other particulars the Authority thinks fit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 6: the Authority's register is as the regulation requires` MEANS
    `the register records the licensee's full name and address, the date the licence was granted and its date of expiry, its registration number, whether the licensee has been convicted of any offence under the Act, whether the licence has been suspended or cancelled or an application to renew refused, and other particulars the Authority thinks fit`

GIVEN `the person pays the appropriate fee specified in the Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 7: the person may inspect the register during the Authority's office hours, or obtain a certified true copy of an entry` MEANS
    `the person pays the appropriate fee specified in the Schedule`

-- src:TA1999-RG4:125 | 8. Every licensee shall —
-- src:TA1999-RG4:126 | (a) carry out any telecommunication cable detection work that he is permitted to
-- src:TA1999-RG4:127 | carry out under his licence in accordance with the conditions of his licence and
-- src:TA1999-RG4:128 | the provisions of the Act and these Regulations;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:129 | (b) on being required by the Authority or a telecommunication system licensee or
-- src:TA1999-RG4:130 | any person authorised by the Authority or the telecommunication system licensee
-- src:TA1999-RG4:131 | for this purpose, produce his licence for examination and furnish such information
-- src:TA1999-RG4:132 | required by it relating to his performance of any telecommunication cable
-- src:TA1999-RG4:133 | detection work;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:134 | (c) if he knows or ought reasonably to know of any damage to any
-- src:TA1999-RG4:135 | telecommunication cable belonging to, or under the management or control of, a
-- src:TA1999-RG4:136 | telecommunication system licensee, immediately inform the telecommunication
-- src:TA1999-RG4:137 | system licensee of the damage by the quickest practicable means;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:138 | (d) immediately inform the Authority in writing of any change in his address; and
-- src:TA1999-RG4:139 | (e) attend at such place as the Authority, or any person authorised by the
-- src:TA1999-RG4:140 | Authority, may specify to produce such documents or furnish such information as
-- src:TA1999-RG4:141 | the Authority or that person may require for the purpose of ensuring compliance
-- src:TA1999-RG4:142 | with the provisions of the Act and these Regulations.
@ref Rg 4 reg 8 (src:TA1999-RG4:125-142)
GIVEN `the licensee carries out the cable detection work in accordance with the conditions of the licence and the Act and these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee produces the licence and furnishes the information required when required by the Authority, a telecommunication system licensee or a person authorised by either` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee immediately informs the telecommunication system licensee of any damage to its cable that the licensee knows or ought reasonably to know of, by the quickest practicable means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee immediately informs the Authority in writing of any change in address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee attends where the Authority specifies to produce documents or furnish information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 8: the licensee has done what the regulation requires` MEANS
        `the licensee carries out the cable detection work in accordance with the conditions of the licence and the Act and these Regulations`
    AND `the licensee produces the licence and furnishes the information required when required by the Authority, a telecommunication system licensee or a person authorised by either`
    AND `the licensee immediately informs the telecommunication system licensee of any damage to its cable that the licensee knows or ought reasonably to know of, by the quickest practicable means`
    AND `the licensee immediately informs the Authority in writing of any change in address`
    AND `the licensee attends where the Authority specifies to produce documents or furnish information`

-- src:TA1999-RG4:145 | 9. For the purpose of ensuring that a licensee is competent to carry out
-- src:TA1999-RG4:146 | telecommunication cable detection work, the Authority may, at any time by notice in
-- src:TA1999-RG4:147 | writing, require the licensee to attend at such time and place specified in the notice to
-- src:TA1999-RG4:148 | take and successfully complete such tests or examinations as the Authority may require.
@ref Rg 4 reg 9 (src:TA1999-RG4:145-148)
GIVEN `the Authority gave written notice requiring the licensee to attend at a time and place to take and complete a test or examination` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 9: the licensee must take and successfully complete the test or examination` MEANS
    `the Authority gave written notice requiring the licensee to attend at a time and place to take and complete a test or examination`

-- src:TA1999-RG4:154 | 10. —(1) In addition to any penalty which may be imposed under these Regulations or
-- src:TA1999-RG4:155 | otherwise, if a licensee —
-- src:TA1999-RG4:156 | (a) has, in the opinion of the Authority, obtained his licence by making or causing
-- src:TA1999-RG4:157 | to be made or produced any false or fraudulent declaration, certificate, or
-- src:TA1999-RG4:158 | representation, in writing or otherwise;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:159 | (b) has been convicted of any offence under the Act or any regulations made
-- src:TA1999-RG4:160 | thereunder, or of any other offence which is of such a nature as to render it, in the
-- src:TA1999-RG4:161 | opinion of the Authority, undesirable that he should continue to hold such licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:162 | (c) contravenes any term or condition of his licence;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:163 | (d) having been given notice under regulation 9 to attend at a specified time and
-- src:TA1999-RG4:164 | place to take a test or an examination as required by the Authority, fails to attend
-- src:TA1999-RG4:165 | at that time or place or fails the test or examination;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:166 | (e) is, in the opinion of the Authority, for any reason incapable of carrying out the
-- src:TA1999-RG4:167 | cable detection work in respect of which the licence was granted;
-- src:TA1999-RG4:168 | (f) applies to have his licence cancelled or suspended; or
-- src:TA1999-RG4:169 | (g) is, in the opinion of the Authority, for any other reason, unfit to hold or to
-- src:TA1999-RG4:170 | continue to hold a licence,
-- src:TA1999-RG4:171 | the Authority may, notwithstanding that the licence has been renewed since the
-- src:TA1999-RG4:172 | occurrence of the relevant event, cancel or refuse to renew a licence or suspend the
-- src:TA1999-RG4:173 | licence for such period as the Authority thinks fit.
-- src:TA1999-RG4:174 | (2) Where a licence is cancelled or suspended, no fee or part thereof shall be refunded by
-- src:TA1999-RG4:175 | the Authority to the licensee in respect of the unexpired period of the licence.
-- src:TA1999-RG4:176 | (3) Without prejudice to paragraph (1), where the Authority is satisfied in any case that a
-- src:TA1999-RG4:177 | licensee has failed to carry out his duties as a telecommunication cable detection worker
-- src:TA1999-RG4:178 | in a safe, careful or proper manner, the Authority may —
-- src:TA1999-RG4:179 | (a) order the licensee to undergo such retraining as the Authority may specify for
-- src:TA1999-RG4:180 | a period not exceeding 12 months; and
-- src:TA1999-RG4:181 | (b) suspend his licence until the licensee has completed the retraining to the
-- src:TA1999-RG4:182 | satisfaction of the Authority.
@ref Rg 4 reg 10 (src:TA1999-RG4:154-182)
GIVEN `in the Authority's opinion the licence was obtained by a false or fraudulent declaration, certificate or representation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee has been convicted of an offence under the Act or its regulations, or another offence that makes it undesirable in the Authority's opinion that the licensee continue to hold the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee contravenes a term or condition of the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee, given notice under regulation 9, fails to attend or fails the test or examination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the Authority's opinion the licensee is for any reason incapable of carrying out the work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee applies to have the licence cancelled or suspended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the Authority's opinion the licensee is for any other reason unfit to hold the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 10(1): the Authority may, notwithstanding that the licence has been renewed since the relevant event, cancel or refuse to renew the licence or suspend it for such period as it thinks fit` MEANS
        `in the Authority's opinion the licence was obtained by a false or fraudulent declaration, certificate or representation`
    OR `the licensee has been convicted of an offence under the Act or its regulations, or another offence that makes it undesirable in the Authority's opinion that the licensee continue to hold the licence`
    OR `the licensee contravenes a term or condition of the licence`
    OR `the licensee, given notice under regulation 9, fails to attend or fails the test or examination`
    OR `in the Authority's opinion the licensee is for any reason incapable of carrying out the work`
    OR `the licensee applies to have the licence cancelled or suspended`
    OR `in the Authority's opinion the licensee is for any other reason unfit to hold the licence`

GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied the licensee failed to carry out his duties in a safe, careful or proper manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 10(2) and (3): the Authority may order retraining of up to 12 months and suspend the licence until completed, and no fee is refunded` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied the licensee failed to carry out his duties in a safe, careful or proper manner`

-- src:TA1999-RG4:185 | 11. The Authority may, at any time and for such reason as it thinks sufficient, reduce the
-- src:TA1999-RG4:186 | period for which a licence has been suspended.
@ref Rg 4 reg 11 (src:TA1999-RG4:185-186)
GIVEN `the Authority thinks the reason sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 11: the Authority may reduce the period of suspension` MEANS
    `the Authority thinks the reason sufficient`

-- src:TA1999-RG4:189 | 12. If any licence is suspended or cancelled, the licensee shall, within 14 days of the date
-- src:TA1999-RG4:190 | of suspension or cancellation, deliver the licence and any duplicate or replacement
-- src:TA1999-RG4:191 | licence to the Authority.
@ref Rg 4 reg 12 (src:TA1999-RG4:189-191)
GIVEN `days after the suspension or cancellation that the licensee delivered the licence and any duplicate or replacement licence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 12: the licensee delivered the licence within time` MEANS
    `days after the suspension or cancellation that the licensee delivered the licence and any duplicate or replacement licence` AT MOST 14

-- src:TA1999-RG4:197 | 13. If the Authority is satisfied that any licence has been lost, destroyed or defaced, the
-- src:TA1999-RG4:198 | Authority may, upon payment of the appropriate fee specified in the Schedule, grant a
-- src:TA1999-RG4:199 | replacement licence.
@ref Rg 4 reg 13 (src:TA1999-RG4:197-199)
GIVEN `the Authority is satisfied the licence was lost, destroyed or defaced and the fee in the Schedule is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 13: the Authority may grant a replacement licence` MEANS
    `the Authority is satisfied the licence was lost, destroyed or defaced and the fee in the Schedule is paid`

-- src:TA1999-RG4:201 | 14. Without prejudice to the right of the Authority to exercise its powers under regulation
-- src:TA1999-RG4:202 | 10, any licensee who —
-- src:TA1999-RG4:203 | (a) contravenes regulation 8 (b), (c), (d) or (e); or
-- src:TA1999-RG4:204 | (b) fails to deliver any licence to the Authority as required under regulation 12,
-- src:TA1999-RG4:205 | shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:TA1999-RG4:206 | $2,000.
@ref Rg 4 reg 14 (src:TA1999-RG4:201-206)
GIVEN `the licensee contravenes regulation 8(b), (c), (d) or (e)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee fails to deliver a licence as regulation 12 requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 4 reg 14: the most the fine may be on conviction, in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the licensee contravenes regulation 8(b), (c), (d) or (e)` OR `the licensee fails to deliver a licence as regulation 12 requires` THEN JUST 2000
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- src:TA1999-RG4:213 | 1. For the grant or renewal of a licence $30
-- src:TA1999-RG4:214 | 2. For the grant of a replacement licence $20
-- src:TA1999-RG4:215 | 3. For inspection of the register $5
-- src:TA1999-RG4:216 | 4. For issue of a certified true copy of an entry in the register $5.
@ref Rg 4 Schedule (src:TA1999-RG4:213-216)
GIVEN item IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 4 Schedule: the fee in dollars` MEANS
    BRANCH IF item EQUALS 1 THEN JUST 30
           IF item EQUALS 2 THEN JUST 20
           IF item EQUALS 3 THEN JUST 5
           IF item EQUALS 4 THEN JUST 5
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `S 477/2005 (in operation 21 July 2005)`

-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:14 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Cable Detection
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:15 | Workers) (Amendment) Regulations 2005 and shall come into operation on 21st July
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:16 | 2005.
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:18 | Deletion and substitution of regulation 3
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:19 | 2. Regulation 3 of the Telecommunications (Cable Detection Workers) Regulations (Rg
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:20 | 4) (referred to in these Regulations as the principal Regulations) is deleted and the
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:21 | following regulation substituted therefor:
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:22 | “Application for licence
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:23 | 3. An application for a licence shall be made to the Authority in such form as the
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:24 | Authority may determine and shall be accompanied by the appropriate fee
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:25 | specified in the Schedule.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:27 | Amendment of regulation 5
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:28 | 3. Regulation 5 of the principal Regulations is amended by deleting paragraph (b) and
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:29 | substituting the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:30 | “(b) remain valid unless cancelled or suspended in accordance with the provisions
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:31 | of the Act or these Regulations; and”.
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:33 | Amendment of regulation 6
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:34 | 4. Regulation 6 of the principal Regulations is amended —
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:35 | (a) by deleting the words “and the date of expiry” in paragraph (b); and
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:36 | (b) by deleting the words “or whether an application to renew the licence has been
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:37 | refused” in paragraph (e).
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:39 | Amendment of regulation 10
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:40 | 5. Regulation 10 (1) of the principal Regulations is amended by deleting the words “,
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:41 | notwithstanding that the licence has been renewed since the occurrence of the relevant
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:42 | event, cancel or refuse to renew a licence or suspend the licence” in the 22nd, 23rd and
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:43 | penultimate lines and substituting the words “cancel or suspend the licence”.
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:45 | Amendment of Schedule
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:46 | 6. Item 1 in the Schedule to the principal Regulations is amended by deleting the words
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:47 | “or renewal”.
@ref Rg 4 as amended by S 477/2005 (src:TA1999-RG4-S477-2005:14-47)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the application is made to the Authority in the form it determined, with the appropriate fee specified in the Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 3 (from 21 July 2005): the application for a licence is as the regulation requires` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the application is made to the Authority in the form it determined, with the appropriate fee specified in the Schedule`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the licence has not been cancelled or suspended in accordance with the Act or these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 5(b) (from 21 July 2005): the licence remains valid` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the licence has not been cancelled or suspended in accordance with the Act or these Regulations`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 6 (from 21 July 2005): the register records the date of expiry and whether an application to renew was refused` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 10(1) (from 21 July 2005): the Authority may refuse to renew a licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`Rg 4 Schedule item 1 (from 21 July 2005): the fee in dollars for the grant of a licence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 21 7 2005) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST 30

§ `S 220/2007 (in operation 1 June 2007)`

-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:16 | 1. These Regulations may be cited as the Telecommunications (Cable Detection
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:17 | Workers) (Amendment) Regulations 2007 and shall come into operation on 1st June 2007.
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:19 | Amendment of regulation 8
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:20 | 2. The Telecommunications (Cable Detection Workers) Regulations (Rg 4) (referred to
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:21 | in these Regulations as the principal Regulations) are amended by renumbering
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:22 | regulation 8 as paragraph (1) of that regulation, and by inserting immediately thereafter
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:23 | the following paragraphs:
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:24 | “(2) It shall be a condition of every licence that the licensee shall carry out his
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:25 | duties as a telecommunication cable detection worker in a safe, careful and proper
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:26 | manner.
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:27 | (3) A licensee shall not cause any telecommunication cable detection work to be
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:28 | carried out by any person, whether employed by him or otherwise, who is not a
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:29 | licensee.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:31 | Amendment of regulation 10
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:32 | 3. Regulation 10 of the principal Regulations is amended by deleting paragraph (3) and
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:33 | substituting the following paragraph:
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:34 | “(3) Where the Authority is satisfied in any case that a licensee has failed to
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:35 | comply with the condition referred to in regulation 8 (2), the Authority may,
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:36 | without prejudice to any other action that it is entitled to take under the Act or
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:37 | these Regulations, order the licensee to undergo such retraining as the Authority
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:38 | may specify for a period not exceeding 12 months.”.
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:39 | Amendment of regulation 14
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:40 | 4. Regulation 14 of the principal Regulations is amended by deleting the words
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:41 | “regulation 8 (b), (c), (d) or (e)” in paragraph (a) and substituting the words “regulation 8
-- src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:42 | (1) (b), (c), (d) or (e) or (3)”.
@ref Rg 4 as amended by S 220/2007 (src:TA1999-RG4-S220-2007:16-42)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the licensee carries out his duties as a telecommunication cable detection worker in a safe, careful and proper manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the licensee causes any cable detection work to be carried out by a person who is not a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 8(2) and (3) (from 1 June 2007): the licensee is meeting the condition and the prohibition` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 6 2007) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (`the licensee carries out his duties as a telecommunication cable detection worker in a safe, careful and proper manner` AND (NOT `the licensee causes any cable detection work to be carried out by a person who is not a licensee`))

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the Authority is satisfied the licensee failed to comply with the condition in regulation 8(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 10(3) (from 1 June 2007): the Authority may order retraining of up to 12 months` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 6 2007) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the Authority is satisfied the licensee failed to comply with the condition in regulation 8(2)`

GIVEN d IS A DATE
      `the licensee contravenes regulation 8(1)(b), (c), (d) or (e) or 8(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Rg 4 reg 14(a) (from 1 June 2007): the licensee is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN (Date 1 6 2007) THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST `the licensee contravenes regulation 8(1)(b), (c), (d) or (e) or 8(3)`
